1	//! Prompt mode: prompts, compiled on demand from Piton, are sent to a local
2	//! coding harness as tasks, and each task's output is shown until it finishes.
3	//!
4	//! The latest task heads the view: its status as a coloured label, the hidden
5	//! anchor it was compiled from, and the compiled prompt the harness received.
6	//! Its output fills the space beneath, one table row per thing the harness
7	//! did (its text, each tool call, any error), with the kind of each as a
8	//! badge. While the task is under way, a skeleton row stands for what the
9	//! harness does next, its parts filled in as they become known. A small row, always shown above the header, expands into a scrollable
10	//! accordion of every task sent, each of which opens onto its own output. A file opened
11	//! from the project tree splits the view, taking half of its width; the chat
12	//! input is never split.
13	//!
14	//! Prompts sent while the harness works wait in a queue, saved with the
15	//! project (see [`crate::prompt_queue`]), listed along the bottom of the view.
16	//!
17	//! Every task is saved with the project too (see [`crate::prompt_history`]),
18	//! and opening the project brings back the tasks sent before.
